+{
+  "exit": 0,
+  "files": {
+    "README.md": "# fraud-detector\n\nReal-time fraud detection service using ML models\n\n## Ownership\n\n| Field | Value |\n| ----- | ----- |\n| Team | risk |\n| Slack | #risk-ml-oncall |\n| PagerDuty | PMLTEAM1 |\n| Runbook | https://wiki/runbooks/fraud-detector |\n\n## Architecture\n\n| Property | Value |\n| -------- | ----- |\n| Tier | critical |\n| Type | ai-gate |\n| Support Model | self |\n| Dependencies | 2 |\n\n## SLOs\n\n| Name | Target | Window | Type |\n| ---- | ------ | ------ | ---- |\n| availability | 99.9 | 30d | availability |\n| latency | 100.0 | 30d | latency |\n| reversal_rate | 0.05 | 7d | availability |\n| high_confidence_failure | 0.01 | 7d | availability |\n\n## Dependencies\n\n| Name | Type | Critical | SLO Availability |\n| ---- | ---- | -------- | ---------------- |\n| feature-store | database | Yes | 99.99 |\n| model-registry | api | No | - |\n\n## Deployment\n\n**Environments:** production, shadow, staging\n\n**Gates:**\n\n- Error Budget: enabled (threshold: 0.15)\n- SLO Compliance: threshold 0.99\n\n## APIs\n\n<!-- TODO: Add API endpoint documentation -->\n\n## Runbook\n\n[Runbook](https://wiki/runbooks/fraud-detector)\n",
+    "adr/001-initial-architecture.md": "# ADR-001: Initial Architecture for fraud-detector\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nfraud-detector is a **critical**-tier **ai-gate** service owned by the **risk** team.\nIt depends on: feature-store, model-registry.\n\n## Decision\n\n- **Tier:** critical — requires highest reliability guarantees\n- **SLO targets:**\n  - availability: 99.9 (30d window)\n  - latency: 100.0 (30d window)\n  - reversal_rate: 0.05 (7d window)\n  - high_confidence_failure: 0.01 (7d window)\n- **Critical dependencies:** feature-store\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Service must maintain SLO targets as defined above\n- Deployment gates enforce error budget thresholds before release\n- On-call rotation required for this tier level\n",
+    "adr/README.md": "# Architecture Decision Records — fraud-detector\n\nThis directory contains architecture decision records (ADRs) for the fraud-detector service.\n\n## Index\n\n| ID | Title | Status |\n| -- | ----- | ------ |\n| 001 | [Initial Architecture](001-initial-architecture.md) | Accepted |\n\n## Creating a New ADR\n\nCopy `template.md` and increment the ID number.\n",
+    "adr/template.md": "# ADR-NNN: Title\n\n## Status\n\nProposed\n\n## Context\n\nWhat is the issue that we're seeing that is motivating this decision or change?\n\n## Decision\n\nWhat is the change that we're proposing and/or doing?\n\n## Consequences\n\nWhat becomes easier or more difficult to do because of this change?\n",
+    "api.md": "# AI Gate Documentation — fraud-detector\n\n## Decision Endpoints\n\n<!-- TODO: Document decision API endpoints -->\n\n### Example Decision Request\n\n```json\n{\n  \"input\": {},\n  \"context\": {}\n}\n```\n\n## Judgment SLOs\n\n- **reversal_rate:** 0.05 (7d window)\n- **high_confidence_failure:** 0.01 (7d window)\n\n## Standard SLOs\n\n- **availability:** 99.9 (30d window)\n- **latency:** 100.0 (30d window)\n"
+  }
+}
